  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "ER1",
      "status": "static_bound",
      "claim": "The concrete normal remainder construction produces a PAudioSegment carrying selected stream, rounded/reconverted start, end-derived nonnegative length, source offset and the event Float32 volume.",
      "addresses": [
        "10020f2e8",
        "100210508..1002105c0",
        "10011376c",
        "101a179cc",
        "101a17ccc",
        "101a17cec",
        "101a17cdc",
        "101a17d14"
      ],
      "details": [
        "PAudioSegment vptr104436be0; stream+38; start+50; length+58; sourceOffset+60; Float32 volume+68.",
        "The end setter subtracts stored start then FMAX with0 before storing length; finite inputs only in this contract.",
        "Coordinates use native datum conversion then sign-selected +/-0.5 and FCVTZS in construction. This is not ties-to-even frame rounding.",
        "The constructor and stores establish segment data, not sample consumption."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ER2",
      "status": "static_bound_with_source_role_dependency",
      "claim": "A source-backed zero effective auto-fade flag word bypasses automatic fades without a builder suppression override.",
      "addresses": [
        "1001f7554",
        "1001fcf1c",
        "101700eb4",
        "101720d58",
        "10018cd6c",
        "10020f708..10020f78c"
      ],
      "details": [
        "Local track+170 nonnull is used directly. Otherwise track+618 tail101700eb4 obtains selected list+30 owner, and101720d58 loads that receiver+c0.",
        "MAutoFadeSetting vtable104440de0 +98 reads u16 into+c, Double into+10, then four expected MInterpolator objects into+18/+20/+28/+30.",
        "Builder10020f740/748 skips automatic fades for nil effective setting or u16+c==0 before duration/interpolator use. Nonzero settings are outside this first subset.",
        "Parent-owned forward probe reaches the MRoot project setting and local track null objects by native reader order; exact source/project role and clone/mutation scope remain in the separate autofade-source finding.",
        "Builder flags0x28 can suppress automatic fades but are not used as source-fidelity evidence. Flags0 and0x80 do not suppress them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ER3",
      "status": "static_bound_conditional",
      "claim": "Null event fade pointers and absent neighbor attributes yield the normal remainder path when effective automatic fades are disabled and the event is otherwise eligible.",
      "addresses": [
        "100212f3c",
        "1000ea79c",
        "1000ea87c",
        "1000ea704",
